# tasks_map_tracker_blocks: More runs than a run block holds (240): 240 single-page runs fill the first block, the next run past them starts a second, and a run inside the full first block splits it. Then an unmap of the whole task (section 7.1): it removes the first block and stops, so the second block's runs stay recorded although the host unmapped them; an object list there is not mapped again, reads the host's zero-filled pages, and its entry is "invalid", while an object list in the first block's range is mapped again and works. Blocks only, for the reason tasks_map_tracker gives.
